                <pb facs="0289" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11229: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-04T14:00:00+08:00">October 4, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>89. Following sent to the Legation: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 4, 1 p.m. Hsuchong, Honan, which has long been occupied by
                            Kuominchun troops and many times reported as captured by National troops
                            is now occupied by latter and held. Also officially announce fall of
                            Kaifeng to government forces.</p>
                        <p>U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Luzon</hi> fired upon at point 45 miles
                            this side Kiukiang on 2nd and returned fire. Steamship <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Ichang</hi> of Yangtze Rapid Company heavily
                            fired upon about 10 miles above Chenglingki on September 29 by rifles
                            and trench mortar. Fire returned by naval armed guard aboard. Repeated
                            to Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
